    "---\n",
    "## Task 2 — Data Preprocessing & Label Alignment <a id='3'></a>\n",
    "\n",
    "### ⚠️ The Subword Challenge\n",
    "\n",
    "BERT tokenizers split words into **subword tokens** (WordPiece). This creates a mismatch between word-level labels and token-level inputs:\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "Word    :  \"Washington\"     → label: B-NP\n",
    "Tokens  :  [\"Washington\"]   → label: [B-NP]          ✅ (single token)\n",
    "\n",
    "Word    :  \"running\"        → label: I-VP\n",
    "Tokens  :  [\"run\",\"##ning\"] → labels: [I-VP, -100]   ✅ (continuation ignored)\n",
    "\n",
    "Special :  [CLS], [SEP]     → labels: [-100, -100]   ✅ (always ignored)\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "**Rules applied:**\n",
    "- First subword of a word → inherits the original word label\n",
    "- Subsequent subwords (`##...`) → assigned `-100` (ignored by cross-entropy)\n",
    "- Special tokens `[CLS]` / `[SEP]` → assigned `-100`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "# TASK 2: TOKENISATION & LABEL ALIGNMENT\n",
    "# Two separate tokenized datasets are created:\n",
    "#   pos_tokenized   → aligned with pos_tags\n",
    "#   chunk_tokenized → aligned with chunk_tags\n",
    "# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "\n",
    "MODEL_CHECKPOINT = \"distilbert-base-uncased\"   # Lighter than BERT; ~66M params\n",
    "MAX_LEN          = 128                          # Max sequence length\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"⏳ Loading tokenizer: '{MODEL_CHECKPOINT}' ...\")\n",
    "tokenizer = AutoTokenizer.from_pretrained(MODEL_CHECKPOINT)\n",
    "print(\"✅ Tokenizer loaded!\")\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def tokenize_and_align_labels(examples: dict, label_column: str) -> dict:\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    Tokenize a batch of sentences and align word-level labels\n",
    "    to the resulting subword tokens.\n",
    "\n",
    "    Strategy:\n",
    "      - First subword of a word   → inherits word label\n",
    "      - Subsequent subwords       → -100  (ignored in loss)\n",
    "      - Special tokens [CLS][SEP] → -100  (ignored in loss)\n",
    "\n",
    "    Parameters\n",
    "    ----------\n",
    "    examples     : dict – Batch of dataset examples.\n",
    "    label_column : str  – 'pos_tags' or 'chunk_tags'.\n",
    "\n",
    "    Returns\n",
    "    -------\n",
    "    dict – Tokenized batch with aligned 'labels' field added.\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    # Tokenize: is_split_into_words=True because tokens are already split\n",
    "    tokenized = tokenizer(\n",
    "        examples[\"tokens\"],\n",
    "        truncation          = True,\n",
    "        max_length          = MAX_LEN,\n",
    "        is_split_into_words = True   # Input is list of words, not a raw string\n",
    "    )\n",
    "\n",
    "    aligned_labels = []\n",
    "\n",
    "    for i, word_labels in enumerate(examples[label_column]):\n",
    "        # word_ids() maps each token index → its source word index\n",
    "        # Returns None for [CLS] and [SEP] special tokens\n",
    "        word_ids     = tokenized.word_ids(batch_index=i)\n",
    "        label_ids    = []\n",
    "        prev_word_id = None\n",
    "\n",
    "        for word_id in word_ids:\n",
    "            if word_id is None:\n",
    "                # Special token: ignore in loss calculation\n",
    "                label_ids.append(-100)\n",
    "            elif word_id != prev_word_id:\n",
    "                # First subword of this word → assign the word's label\n",
    "                label_ids.append(word_labels[word_id])\n",
    "            else:\n",
    "                # Continuation subword → ignore in loss\n",
    "                label_ids.append(-100)\n",
    "\n",
    "            prev_word_id = word_id\n",
    "\n",
    "        aligned_labels.append(label_ids)\n",
    "\n",
    "    tokenized[\"labels\"] = aligned_labels\n",
    "    return tokenized\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"✅ tokenize_and_align_labels() defined.\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── Demonstrate label alignment on one example ────────────────\n",
    "demo     = raw_datasets[\"train\"][0]\n",
    "demo_enc = tokenizer(\n",
    "    demo[\"tokens\"],\n",
    "    is_split_into_words = True,\n",
    "    truncation          = True,\n",
    "    max_length          = MAX_LEN\n",
    ")\n",
    "word_ids      = demo_enc.word_ids()\n",
    "subword_tokens = tokenizer.convert_ids_to_tokens(demo_enc[\"input_ids\"])\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\n── Label Alignment Demo (first 12 subword tokens) ──\")\n",
    "demo_align_df = pd.DataFrame({\n",
    "    \"Subword Token\" : subword_tokens[:12],\n",
    "    \"Word ID\"       : [str(w) for w in word_ids[:12]],\n",
    "    \"Aligned POS\"   : [\n",
    "        POS_LABELS[demo[\"pos_tags\"][w]] if w is not None else \"[SPECIAL → -100]\"\n",
    "        for w in word_ids[:12]\n",
    "    ]\n",
    "})\n",
    "display(demo_align_df)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ── Apply tokenisation to all splits for BOTH tasks ──────────\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"⏳ Tokenizing and aligning POS labels...\")\n",
    "pos_tokenized = raw_datasets.map(\n",
    "    lambda ex: tokenize_and_align_labels(ex, \"pos_tags\"),\n",
    "    batched        = True,\n",
    "    remove_columns = raw_datasets[\"train\"].column_names   # Drop raw text columns\n",
    ")\n",
    "print(\"   → POS tokenized dataset ready\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"⏳ Tokenizing and aligning Chunk labels...\")\n",
    "chunk_tokenized = raw_datasets.map(\n",
    "    lambda ex: tokenize_and_align_labels(ex, \"chunk_tags\"),\n",
    "    batched        = True,\n",
    "    remove_columns = raw_datasets[\"train\"].column_names\n",
    ")\n",
    "print(\"   → Chunk tokenized dataset ready\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── Verify output fields ──────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "print(\"\\n── Tokenized features ──\")\n",
    "print(pos_tokenized[\"train\"].features)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\n── First example output (first 10 positions) ──\")\n",
    "print(\"input_ids     :\", pos_tokenized[\"train\"][0][\"input_ids\"][:10])\n",
    "print(\"attention_mask:\", pos_tokenized[\"train\"][0][\"attention_mask\"][:10])\n",
    "print(\"labels        :\", pos_tokenized[\"train\"][0][\"labels\"][:10])\n",
    "print(\"\\nNote: -100 = special/continuation token (excluded from loss)\")"
   ]
  },
