   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## Task 4 — Training <a id='5'></a>\n",
    "\n",
    "We use the Hugging Face `Trainer` API which handles:\n",
    "- Dynamic padding via `DataCollatorForTokenClassification`\n",
    "- Mixed-precision (FP16) if GPU is available\n",
    "- Gradient clipping and accumulation\n",
    "- Checkpoint saving and best-model restoration\n",
    "\n",
    "**Hyperparameters:**\n",
    "\n",
    "| Parameter | Value | Rationale |\n",
    "|---|---|---|\n",
    "| Learning rate | 2e-5 | Standard for BERT/DistilBERT fine-tuning |\n",
    "| Epochs | 3 | Sufficient for CoNLL-2003 convergence |\n",
    "| Batch size | 16 | Fits most GPU/CPU environments |\n",
    "| Weight decay | 0.01 | L2 regularisation prevents overfitting |\n",
    "| Warmup ratio | 0.1 | 10% of steps as linear LR warmup |"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "# TASK 4: TRAINING SETUP UTILITIES\n",
    "# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "\n",
    "# DataCollator: pads each batch dynamically to its longest sequence\n",
    "# (more memory-efficient than padding everything to MAX_LEN)\n",
    "data_collator  = DataCollatorForTokenClassification(tokenizer)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Load seqeval for span-level metric computation\n",
    "seqeval_metric = evaluate.load(\"seqeval\")\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def make_compute_metrics(id2label: dict):\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    Factory: returns a compute_metrics function bound to a specific id2label.\n",
    "    The Trainer calls this after each evaluation epoch.\n",
    "\n",
    "    seqeval evaluates complete entity/phrase spans — stricter than\n",
    "    token-level accuracy (a span is correct only if ALL tokens match).\n",
    "\n",
    "    Parameters\n",
    "    ----------\n",
    "    id2label : dict – int → label string mapping.\n",
    "\n",
    "    Returns\n",
    "    -------\n",
    "    compute_metrics : callable – takes EvalPrediction, returns metric dict.\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    def compute_metrics(eval_pred):\n",
    "        logits, labels = eval_pred\n",
    "\n",
    "        # Convert logits → predicted class IDs (argmax over label dimension)\n",
    "        predictions = np.argmax(logits, axis=-1)\n",
    "\n",
    "        # Convert IDs → string labels, skipping -100 positions\n",
    "        true_labels = [\n",
    "            [id2label[l] for l in label_row if l != -100]\n",
    "            for label_row in labels\n",
    "        ]\n",
    "        true_preds  = [\n",
    "            [id2label[p] for p, l in zip(pred_row, label_row) if l != -100]\n",
    "            for pred_row, label_row in zip(predictions, labels)\n",
    "        ]\n",
    "\n",
    "        # seqeval expects lists-of-lists of label strings\n",
    "        results = seqeval_metric.compute(\n",
    "            predictions = true_preds,\n",
    "            references  = true_labels\n",
    "        )\n",
    "        return {\n",
    "            \"precision\" : round(results[\"overall_precision\"], 4),\n",
    "            \"recall\"    : round(results[\"overall_recall\"],    4),\n",
    "            \"f1\"        : round(results[\"overall_f1\"],        4),\n",
    "            \"accuracy\"  : round(results[\"overall_accuracy\"],  4),\n",
    "        }\n",
    "\n",
    "    return compute_metrics\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def make_training_args(output_dir: str,\n",
    "                       epochs: int     = 3,\n",
    "                       lr: float       = 2e-5,\n",
    "                       batch_size: int = 16) -> TrainingArguments:\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    Build Hugging Face TrainingArguments for token classification.\n",
    "\n",
    "    Parameters\n",
    "    ----------\n",
    "    output_dir : str   – Where to save checkpoints.\n",
    "    epochs     : int   – Number of training epochs.\n",
    "    lr         : float – AdamW learning rate.\n",
    "    batch_size : int   – Per-device batch size for train and eval.\n",
    "\n",
    "    Returns\n",
    "    -------\n",
    "    TrainingArguments\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    return TrainingArguments(\n",
    "        output_dir                  = output_dir,\n",
    "        num_train_epochs            = epochs,\n",
    "        learning_rate               = lr,\n",
    "        per_device_train_batch_size = batch_size,\n",
    "        per_device_eval_batch_size  = batch_size,\n",
    "        weight_decay                = 0.01,        # L2 regularisation\n",
    "        warmup_ratio                = 0.1,         # 10% linear warmup\n",
    "        eval_strategy               = \"epoch\",     # Evaluate after every epoch\n",
    "        save_strategy               = \"epoch\",     # Save checkpoint every epoch\n",
    "        load_best_model_at_end      = True,        # Restore best checkpoint\n",
    "        metric_for_best_model       = \"f1\",        # Use F1 to select best model\n",
    "        logging_steps               = 100,\n",
    "        seed                        = SEED,\n",
    "        report_to                   = \"none\"       # Disable wandb/mlflow\n",
    "    )\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"✅ Training utilities ready (data_collator, compute_metrics, training_args).\")"
   ]
  },
